{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Make for yourself, etc.</b> One needs to know why the trumpets were necessary for the journeying of the camps — were not the eyes of all Israel upon the cloud, and when they saw it move they would move? Perhaps it is because they did not travel all at once, but rather the banner of Judah would go first, and after them the sons of Gershon bearing the Tabernacle, and after them the banner of Reuben, and so on — therefore the trumpets were needed so that each one would know the precise time at which to set out, this one after that one. Further, it appears from a fine point in the verse's additional saying of the word <b>lekha</b>, which should not have been necessary, and it will be explained according to the words of our Sages, whose memory is for a blessing, which we wrote nearby, that the cloud would not lift up until Moses would say to it ״קוּמָה״ and so on, and the matter was dependent on Moses' hand. From this we may also say that HaShem directed that just so, the journeying of Israel would be at Moses' word, for the honor of Moses, in the same way that He granted him the honor regarding the journeying of the cloud, that it would not move until he would say to it ״קוּמָה״ — and this is what is alluded to in the word <b>lekha</b>, meaning: within your domain and by your word. And our Sages, whose memory is for a blessing, expounded (Sifrei here): ״עֲשֵׂה לְךָ״ — from your own resources. They also expounded (Numbers Rabbah 15:15): ״לְךָ״ — you may use them, and no one else may use them. And there are seventy faces to the Torah."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:14.790464411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}